  <description>
    <p>Multiplies connected inputs.</p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Module</td>
          <td>
            <code>nflow_blocks</code>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Library</td>
          <td>Math blocks</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Type</td>
          <td>
            <code>mult</code>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Label</td>
          <td>Mult</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      <img src="../../../../libraries/math/exports/mult.svg" align="middle"/>
    </p>
    <p>
      <b>Description</b>
    </p>
    <p>Multiplies or divides connected inputs in element-wise or matrix mode. The Inputs parameter specifies the operation for each port.</p>
    <p>In matrix mode, a nonscalar divisor must be square and use single or double precision. Convert integer inputs before matrix division.</p>
    <p>A singular matrix divisor stops simulation with a diagnostic. Generated C and Rust models signal a singular divisor with NaN output values; their step function has no error return.</p>
    <p>
      <b>Ports</b>
    </p>
    <p>Input ports are arranged according to the configured operations.</p>
    <p>
      <b>Output(s)</b>
    </p>
    <p>One output carries the result.</p>
    <p>
      <b>Parameters</b>
    </p>
    <p>Inputs selects multiplication or division for each port. Multiplication selects element-wise or matrix operations.</p>
    <p>
      <b>Block Characteristics</b>
    </p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Block type</td>
